body:
One of the most annoying thing in the React InstantSearch codebase is to conditionally support single and multi index states. I thought we were going to a different structure in InstantSearch.js that will make development easier: always have the index ID as key and remove all top-level states.

```ts
interface IndexUiState {
  query?: string;
  // ...
}

interface UiState {
  [indexId: string]: IndexUiState;
}
```

An example would be:

```ts
const state: UiState = {
  movies: {
    query: 'hammer',
  },
  songs: {
    query: 'burning',
  },
};
```

The role of state mapping would be to transform any single-index mapping to a `IndexUiState` to keep routing backward compatible.
